# WordPress PHP Conventions

See `launchdek-compliance.mdc` for the security gate.

## File Header

Every PHP file must start with:

```php
<?php
/**
 * Brief description.
 *
 * @package LaunchDek
 */

if ( ! defined( 'ABSPATH' ) ) {
	exit;
}
```

## Security

- Admin pages: `LAUNCHDEK_Capabilities::current_user_can( $cap )` — not raw `manage_options` except in capability class itself.
- REST routes: `permission_callback` on every route; delegate to `LAUNCHDEK_REST_API::can_*()` methods.
- Escape output: `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`, `esc_html__()`, `esc_html_e()`.
- Sanitize settings via `LAUNCHDEK_Settings::sanitize()` as `sanitize_callback`.
- Settings API: `show_in_rest => false`.
- Never return decrypted app passwords in REST responses; mask or omit `app_password_enc`.
- SQL: `$wpdb->prepare()` only; all queries in `*_Repository` classes.

## WordPress APIs

- Register hooks in `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin::run()` or static `::register()` on service classes — not in bootstrap.
- REST namespace: `LAUNCHDEK_REST_NAMESPACE` (`launchdek/v1`).
- Enqueue assets with `filemtime()` fallback to `LAUNCHDEK_VERSION`.
- Localize `launchdekAdmin` with `rest_url()`, `wp_create_nonce( 'wp_rest' )`, and translatable strings. On the Checklists screen, also localize `customChecklists` (`preloaded` + `summary_list` items for non-template checklists).
- Page slugs: use `LAUNCHDEK_Admin::PAGE_SLUG` + suffixes.

## Class Wiring

- Bootstrap requires all classes; instantiate only via `launchdek_run_plugin()`. `class-launchdek-admin-deep-links.php` loads before checklist/run repositories (used during step normalization).
- `LAUNCHDEK_Plugin` constructor: `LAUNCHDEK_Admin` only.
- Data layer: `LAUNCHDEK_{Site,Checklist,Run}_Repository` — no direct `$wpdb` in REST handlers or admin.
- Remote: `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client::from_site( $id )` for authenticated requests (returns `null` if credentials missing). `request()` tries `/wp-json{route}` then `?rest_route=` when `is_rest_no_route_response()` (404 + `rest_no_route` code).
- Client panel: `LAUNCHDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::ensure_installed( $site_id )` on site create/update/test and when `push_run( $id, $prepare, $sync_bundle )` is called with `$sync_bundle = true` (defaults to `$prepare`; manual refresh uses `push_run( $id, false, true )`); `::sync_run()` → `push_run( $id, false, false )` (snapshot only, no bundle reinstall); token callbacks pass `$skip_client_sync = true` on `complete_client_step()` / `uncomplete_client_step()` / `add_client_step_note()` and return `snapshot` for client local apply; `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::ensure_client_token()` backfills legacy runs; `::filter_step_notes()` / `::step_notes_match()` dedupe hub notes; `::archive()` / `::delete()` for run history (`is_archived` soft-hide); `::list_for_site_history()` for paginated lean site history with batched step progress; `LAUNCHDEK_Step_Executor::mark_manual_incomplete()` for hub-side manual uncomplete; `LAUNCHDEK_Auto_Capture::{get_status,start,stop,clear}()` proxies capture sessions to remote panel; `LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_layout()` / `::get_client_panel_layouts()` configure snapshot `panel_layout` (legacy `left_sidebar` / `split_panel` sanitize to `sidebar`); `::get_client_panel_title()` / `::sanitize_client_panel_title()` configure snapshot `panel_title`; `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::{resolve_path,normalize_stored_path,infer_path_from_text,path_from_api_step}()` resolve wp-admin paths for step deep links; snapshots include both `deep_link` (remote full URL) and `admin_path` (path only for client `admin_url()` rebuild). Client `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::get_panel_title()` reads snapshot `panel_title`.
- Credentials: `LAUNCHDEK_Credential_Vault::encrypt()` / `::decrypt()` on save/read.
- Audit: `LAUNCHDEK_Audit_Log::log()` for privileged actions; `::feed_entry_show_site_label()` / `::format_feed_message( $entry, $embed_site )` shape dashboard feed copy; `::log()` invalidates `LAUNCHDEK_Dashboard_Cache::invalidate_feed()`.
- Dashboard cache: `LAUNCHDEK_Dashboard_Cache::{get_stats,get_connection_counts,get_feed,get_quick_launch_picker}()` read from `launchdek_dashboard_cache`; `::refresh_quick_launch_picker()` delegates to `LAUNCHDEK_Site_Repository::picker_list()` and `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::picker_list()`; repositories call `invalidate_stats()` / `invalidate_connections()` / `invalidate_quick_launch_picker()` on mutations. `::clear()` on uninstall.
- Checklist summaries: `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository::summary_list( $args )` / `::format_summary()` return lightweight rows (`id`, `title`, `description`, `steps_count`, step id/title preview) for list/grid UIs; `GET /checklists?summary=1` (optional `is_template`, `is_vault`); `GET /templates/vault` uses `summary_list( [ 'is_vault' => true ] )`.
- Activation: `LAUNCHDEK_Activator` (sets redirect transient); `LAUNCHDEK_Admin::maybe_activation_redirect()` sends new installs to dashboard with `?onboarding=1`. Deactivation: `LAUNCHDEK_Deactivator` (clears drift cron).
- Legacy redirects (`LAUNCHDEK_Admin::maybe_redirect_legacy_templates_page()` on `admin_init`): `?page={slug}-templates` → Checklists (Templates default tab); `?page={slug}-sites&activity_logs` → Activity Logs page.

## Settings Option Shape

```php
array(
	'enabled'                    => true,
	'encrypt_credentials'        => true,
	'drift_verification_enabled'  => true,
	'onboarding_dismissed'       => false, // set via POST /onboarding/dismiss; cleared via POST /onboarding/reset
	'slack_webhook'              => '',
	'discord_webhook'            => '',
	'teams_webhook'              => '',
	'notification_events'        => array( 'run_started', 'run_completed', 'run_failed', 'step_failed' ), // also supports drift_detected, client_step_completed, client_note_added — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_notification_events()
	'role_permissions'           => array(), // cap => array of role slugs
	'telemetry_sync_rules'       => array(), // array of { id, enabled } — see LAUNCHDEK_Integrations::get_default_telemetry_rules()
	'exclude_options'            => array( 'url', 'email', 'wp_environment_type' ), // REST field names; legacy option names normalized on save — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_exclude_options()
	'client_panel_layout'        => 'sidebar', // panel display mode on remote wp-admin — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_layouts()
	'client_panel_title'         => 'Agency Checklist', // panel heading on remote wp-admin — see LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_client_panel_title()
)
```

## Checklist Step Types

Steps live in `checklist.steps[]` (JSON in DB or template files).

**`manual`** — fields: `id`, `title`, `instructions`, `target_roles` (optional array of WP role slugs — UI metadata for agency assignment), `deep_link` (optional admin path — stored via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::normalize_stored_path()`; backfilled via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` on save when empty), `show_note_field` (optional bool, default `true` — when `false`, client panel hides the per-step note textarea), `show_screenshot_field` (optional bool, default `true` when notes enabled — when `false`, client panel hides the screenshot attach button), `type: manual`. Executor sets status `awaiting_manual` and resolves admin path via `LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links::resolve_path()` then `LAUNCHDEK_Remote_Client::admin_link()`. User completes via `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete`; revert via `/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete`.

**Step notes** (stored on run steps in hub `launchdek_run_steps.notes_json` + client snapshots) — array of `{ user, text, created_at, attachment_id?, attachment_url? }`. Notes require non-empty `text`. Hub persistence via `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::add_step_note()` / `sanitize_step_note()`. Optional attachments reference existing remote media library IDs; hub stores sanitized `attachment_url` for display in Automation run tracker.

**`api`** — executed by `LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper::execute()` using nested `api` object:

```php
array(
	'type'  => 'api',
	'title' => 'Step title',
	'api'   => array(
		'route'   => '/wp/v2/settings', // must start with /
		'method'  => 'GET',             // GET|POST|PUT|PATCH|DELETE
		'payload' => array(),           // request body for mutating methods
	),
)
```

Validate dry-runs with `LAUNCHDEK_Payload_Mapper::validate()` (used by `/checklists/{id}/validate-step`) — returns `{ valid, errors, warnings }`. `execute()` and `validate()` call `filter_excluded_payload()` for mutating `/wp/v2/settings` steps; stripped keys are omitted from the remote payload and surfaced as warnings (or `WP_Error` when all fields are excluded).

## Admin Deep Links (`LAUNCHDEK_Admin_Deep_Links`)

Resolves wp-admin paths for checklist step settings shortcuts (hub run tracker + client panel `.launchdek-client-step-settings-link`).

| Method | Role |
|--------|------|
| `resolve_path( $step )` | Full resolution: explicit `deep_link` → API inference → `infer_path_from_text()` |
| `normalize_stored_path( $path )` | Sanitize stored admin paths (not `esc_url_raw()` — preserves `options-general.php` style paths) |
| `infer_path_from_text( $title, $instructions )` | Keyword/regex rules for common screens (Permalinks, Plugins, Users, etc.) |
| `path_from_api_step( $api )` | Map `/wp/v2/settings` and other core REST routes to admin screens |

On checklist save, `LAUNCHDEK_Checklist_Repository` normalizes `deep_link` and backfills via `resolve_path()` when empty. Builder live inference uses `POST /checklists/infer-deep-link` (`LAUNCHDEK_REST_API::infer_deep_link()` → `resolve_path()`). `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Push::build_snapshot()` sets `deep_link` (remote full URL) and `admin_path` (path only). Client `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::resolve_step_deep_link()` prefers the snapshot URL, then rebuilds from `admin_path`. `LAUNCHDEK_Templates::repair_builtin_deep_links()` runs once (`launchdek_deep_links_repaired`) to restore built-in template paths stripped by legacy sanitization.

## Built-in Template JSON

Files in `templates/{slug}.json`. Required fields:

```php
array(
	'title'       => 'Template title',
	'description' => 'Short summary',
	'category'    => 'security', // slug from LAUNCHDEK_Templates::get_categories()
	'version'     => '1.0.0',
	'is_template' => true,
	'steps'       => array( /* manual|api step objects */ ),
)
```

Unknown categories fall back to `maintenance`. New JSON files are picked up by `sync_builtin()` without re-seeding.

## DB Upgrades

`LAUNCHDEK_Installer::DB_VERSION` is `1.4.0`. `maybe_install()` calls `migrate_from_previous()` before `install()`. Do not reference `launchdek_workflows` or `workflow_id` in new code — use `launchdek_checklists` and `checklist_id`. Migration to 1.2.0 adds `launchdek_sites.client_agent` and `launchdek_runs.client_run_token`. Migration to 1.3.0 adds `launchdek_run_steps.notes_json` (JSON array of step notes). Migration to 1.4.0 adds `launchdek_runs.is_archived` (indexed tinyint; archive hides from default history). Hub notes persist via `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::add_step_note()` / `update_step( …, [ 'notes' => … ] )`. `LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::all()` excludes archived runs unless `include_archived` is true. Audit log and webhooks accept legacy `workflow_*` action keys and `details.workflow` for pre-migration entries. Client panel audit actions: `client_run_pushed`, `client_step_completed`, `client_step_uncompleted`, `client_step_note_added`, `manual_step_uncompleted`, `run_archived`, `run_deleted`.

## Partials

All non-settings pages use `render_page()` which passes `$settings`, `$page`, and sets `data-launchdek-page` on `.launchdek-admin` root.

| Partial | `$page` value |
|---------|---------------|
| `launchdek-admin-page.php` | `dashboard` (receives `$dashboard_stats`, `$connection_counts`, `$log_feed`, `$quick_launch_picker` from cache; Quick Launch selects pre-rendered with `data-launchdek-preloaded="1"`) |
| `launchdek-sites-page.php` | `sites` |
| `launchdek-activity-logs-page.php` | `activity-logs` (hidden submenu; `GET /logs/feed?detailed=1`, `can_view_dashboard`) |
| `launchdek-checklists-page.php` | `checklists` (four nav tabs: Templates, My Checklists, New Checklist, Auto-Capture) |
| `launchdek-automation-page.php` | `automation` |
| `launchdek-integrations-page.php` | `integrations` |
| `launchdek-settings-page.php` | `settings` (Settings API form) |

Shared modal partials (included via `require`, not `$page`-routed):

| Partial | Included on |
|---------|-------------|
| `launchdek-onboarding-modal.php` | dashboard, settings |
| `launchdek-template-picker-modal.php` | dashboard, checklists, settings |
| `launchdek-confirm-modal.php` | sites |

Document `@var` annotations at the top of page partials.

## Settings Page Sections

Settings partial (`launchdek-settings-page.php`) uses Settings API form with cards. `onboarding_dismissed` is REST-only (`POST /onboarding/dismiss|reset`) — not a Settings form checkbox (saving settings does not reset or toggle it).
- **Platform** — `enabled`, `drift_verification_enabled`
- **Credential Vault Security** — `encrypt_credentials` toggle
- **Exclude Options** — `#launchdek-exclude-options` textarea (`exclude_options`; one REST field or legacy option name per line; defaults `url`, `email`, `wp_environment_type`; aliases via `get_exclude_option_aliases()` / `normalize_exclude_option()`)
- **Client Checklist Panel** — `#launchdek-panel-layout` select (`client_panel_layout`; layouts from `get_client_panel_layouts()` — `sidebar`, `live_topbar`, `bottom_dock`, `floating_pill`, `toast`, `admin_menu`, `fullscreen`, `focus_mode`, `inline_metabox`; legacy `left_sidebar` / `split_panel` sanitize to `sidebar`); live preview via `#launchdek-panel-layout-preview` (`initPanelLayoutPreview()`); `#launchdek-client-panel-title` text input (`client_panel_title`, default `Agency Checklist`, max 80 chars — syncs on next push or panel refresh)
- **Notification Channels** — Slack/Teams/Discord webhooks + event checkboxes (`LAUNCHDEK_Settings::get_notification_events()`)
- **Agency Role Guardrails** — preset cards (`get_agency_role_presets()`) + role-permission matrix (`role_permissions`)
- **Onboarding** — `#launchdek-show-onboarding` button; requires shared onboarding + template-picker modal partials below the form

Telemetry sync rules are managed on the Integrations page (REST), not the Settings form.

Onboarding REST handlers in `LAUNCHDEK_REST_API`:
- `POST /onboarding/dismiss` → `dismiss_onboarding()` (`can_view_dashboard`) — sets `onboarding_dismissed` to `true`
- `POST /onboarding/reset` → `reset_onboarding()` (`can_manage_settings`) — sets `onboarding_dismissed` to `false` for Settings preview

Client panel REST handlers in `LAUNCHDEK_REST_API`:
- `GET /panel/bootstrap` → `get_panel_bootstrap()` (`can_manage_sites`) — returns mu-plugin loader file for manual download
- `POST /sites/{id}/panel/install` → `install_site_panel()` (`can_manage_sites`) — retries `LAUNCHDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::ensure_installed()` (Sites modal **Retry panel install**)
- `GET /sites/{id}/runs` → `get_site_runs()` (`can_manage_sites`) — checklist run history for expandable Sites page rows via `list_for_site_history()` (optional `status`, `limit` default 25 max 200, `offset`; returns `{ runs, has_more, offset, limit }`)
- `POST /runs/{id}/archive` → `archive_run()` (`can_manage_sites`) — soft-hide run from default history (`LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::archive()`)
- `DELETE /runs/{id}` → `delete_run()` (`can_manage_sites`) — permanently delete run and step rows (`LAUNCHDEK_Run_Repository::delete()`)
- `GET|POST|DELETE /sites/{id}/capture` → `get_site_capture()` / `update_site_capture()` / `clear_site_capture()` (`can_edit_checklists`) — proxies to `LAUNCHDEK_Auto_Capture`
- `POST /runs` → optional `push_to_client` (bool, default `true`); when set, calls `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Push::push_run()` after start
- `POST /runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete` → `uncomplete_manual_step()` (`can_execute`) — `LAUNCHDEK_Step_Executor::mark_manual_incomplete()` then `sync_run()`
- `POST /runs/{id}/push-client` → `push_run_to_client()` (`can_execute`) — `push_run( $id, false, true )` snapshot re-push + bundle sync, no auto-advance (Automation **Refresh Client Panel**)
- `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/complete` → `client_complete_step()` (`can_client_token_access_run`) — `complete_client_step( …, true )` (`$skip_client_sync`); returns `snapshot`
- `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/uncomplete` → `client_uncomplete_step()` (`can_client_token_access_run`) — `uncomplete_client_step( …, true )`; returns `snapshot`
- `POST /client-runs/{id}/steps/{step}/notes` → `client_add_step_note()` (`can_client_token_access_run`) — `add_client_step_note( …, true )`; returns `snapshot`
- Run advance handlers (`/next`, `/auto`, manual complete/uncomplete) call `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Push::sync_run()` when panel is available

Remote mu-plugin REST (`mu-plugin/launchdek-client/class-rest-api.php`, namespace `launchdek/v1`):
- `GET /client/info` — public panel probe
- `POST /client/install` — hub pushes whitelisted bundle files (`can_hub_manage` via Application Password)
- `GET|POST|DELETE /client/run` — active run snapshot CRUD
- `POST /client/run/dismiss` — clear completed checklist from client panel (local snapshot only)
- `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/complete` — client user completes step; callbacks to hub with run token
- `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/uncomplete` — client user reverts completed manual step; callbacks to hub with run token
- `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/notes` — saves note locally via `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::add_step_note()`, then syncs to hub (`hub_synced` flag); notes require non-empty text; optional `attachment_id`/`attachment_url` from remote `wp.media`
- `GET|POST|DELETE /client/capture` — auto-capture session status, start/stop, clear captured steps

Client `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::save()` merges local notes with incoming hub snapshots via `merge_step_notes()`; `patch_from_hub_run()` preserves local note data on partial hub responses. Client panel assets in `mu-plugin/launchdek-client/{css,js}/` — prefix selectors with `.launchdek-client-*`; localize `launchdekClient` global.

When editing the client panel bundle, keep hub installer paths (`LAUNCHDEK_Mu_Plugin_Installer::BUNDLE_DIR`) and remote loader (`mu-plugin/launchdek-client.php`) in sync.

## New Integration Checklist

1. Create `includes/integrations/class-launchdek-integration-{slug}.php` implementing `LAUNCHDEK_Integration_Interface`.
2. Register in `LAUNCHDEK_Integrations::get_all()`.
3. Add platform field mappings in `LAUNCHDEK_Integrations::get_default_telemetry_rules()` if connector exposes sync fields.
4. Push agent via existing `/integrations/{slug}/push` route; telemetry rules via `/integrations/telemetry-rules`.

## Docblocks

Document public methods with `@param`, `@return`, and `@var` on class properties.
